# Dawnhand Dissident's casts need "three counters from among creatures you control" (CR 118.3: a cost can't be paid without the
# resources to pay it fully), and once begun a cast does not need the Dissident any more (the ruling: "If ... it's destroyed in
# response, the spell will still resolve normally"). Bot1's turn-three surveil blights its Walking Ballista, whose +1/+1 and -1/-1
# counters cancel (CR 704.5q) and which dies a 0/0, putting Llanowar Elves into the graveyard; on turn five the Elves are exiled
# with the Caryatid blighted twice. With only those two counters among its creatures and {G}{G} open, Bot1 can't cast the Elves:
# the +1/+1 counter on Bot2's Walking Ballista is not on a creature Bot1 controls.
# On turn seven the Dissident blights itself to surveil again: three counters, and the Elves are cast. Bot2 bolts the Dissident in
# response; the Elves resolve all the same.

